      <reaction compartment="compartment_70101" fast="false" id="reaction_192061" metaid="metaid_84" name="CYP46A1 24-hydroxylates CHOL" reversible="false">
        <notes>
          <p xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Cholesterol 24-hydroxylase (CYP46A1), an enzyme associated with the ER membrane, catalyses the 24-hydroxylation of cholesterol (CHOL) to 24-hydroxycholesterol (24OH-CHOL). In the body, this enzyme is expressed predominantly in the brain and is thought to play a major role in cholesterol turnover there (Lund et al. 1999, Mast et al. 2003).</p>
        </notes>
        <annotation>
          <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:vCard="http://www.w3.org/2001/vcard-rdf/3.0#" xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:bqmodel="http://biomodels.net/model-qualifiers/" xmlns:bqbiol="http://biomodels.net/biology-qualifiers/">
